<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 05:17:53 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Oil prices extend gains as US-Iran tensions flare again</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again</link><description>
Oil prices rose further Tuesday as renewed military exchanges between the United States and Iran, coupled with Donald Trump’s vow to hit Tehran “hard,” fueled fears of a broader escalation after weeks of relative calm. Follow our live blog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8c81e48-a591-11f1-9a26-2d6b79c37be8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 03:38:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv kills at least seven</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four</link><description>
A massive Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv and its surrounding region killed at least seven people and wounded more than a dozen overnight, Ukrainian officials said Tuesday, as children prepared to return to school amid heightened fears of further strikes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3254e58-a5ab-11f1-a88b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242478432296.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3254e58-a5ab-11f1-a88b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242478432296.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99553aa0-a5ac-11f1-ac37-232b90c8c885</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 02:26:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3254e58-a5ab-11f1-a88b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26242478432296.jpg">© Francisco Seco, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>Duane “Keffe D” Davis found guilty in Tupac Shakur murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-duane-keffe-d-davis-found-guilty-in-tupac-shakur-murder</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">e18c2c5a-a59f-11f1-b25c-87e6ac0d77a5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:57:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Duane “Keffe D” Davis found guilty in Tupac Shakur murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260901-duane-keffe-d-davis-found-guilty-in-tupac-shakur-murder</link><description>
Duane “Keffe D” Davis was found guilty Monday of orchestrating the 1996 murder of rap icon Tupac Shakur, becoming the first person convicted in the decades-old case. The 63-year-old faces a possible life sentence after a Las Vegas jury deliberated for less than three hours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a6e66d0-a59f-11f1-a753-87e6ac0d77a5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:53:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/18f9a702-a59c-11f1-8391-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243678304338.jpg">© Steve Marcus/Pool Reuters via AP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU suspends Brazilian meat imports over antibiotic compliance concerns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-eu-suspends-brazilian-meat-imports-over-antibiotic-compliance-concerns</link><description>
The European Union will suspend imports of Brazilian meat and other animal products from Thursday, citing concerns over Brazil’s compliance with EU rules on antibiotic use in livestock. The move affects poultry, beef, eggs and honey, with Brussels offering no timeline for when trade can resume.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc257d22-a599-11f1-9c0e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25216715663865.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc257d22-a599-11f1-9c0e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25216715663865.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">192a28ca-a59a-11f1-8a08-e9c5ca52cd69</guid><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:14:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc257d22-a599-11f1-9c0e-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25216715663865.jpg">© Eraldo Peres, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Melting Himalayas? Nepal disaster exposes growing risk of glacial flooding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260831-melting-himalayas-nepal-disaster-exposes-growing-risk-of-glacial-flooding</link><description>
One of the tragic consequences of global warming. Scientists will tell us whether receding glaciers are to blame for last Wednesday’s ice shelf collapse that triggered a catastrophic flood, cascading down more than 3,000 meters from the Chinese border into Nepal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/249699be-a563-11f1-a85a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T171033Z-78116127-RC2Y8NA7BWYN-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/249699be-a563-11f1-a85a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T171033Z-78116127-RC2Y8NA7BWYN-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cd2dd5b4-a55a-11f1-a457-7f5203728eaa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:35:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Glacial flood death toll surpasses 900 in Nepal and Tibet</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260831-glacial-flood-death-toll-surpasses-900-in-nepal-and-tibet</link><description>
Rescuers battled mud and debris Monday as the death toll from devastating glacial floods along the China-Nepal border topped 900, with nearly 4,500 people still missing. Rescue teams continued a desperate search for survivors as entire communities were swept away.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c71ef2e6-a593-11f1-b096-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243178528758.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c71ef2e6-a593-11f1-b096-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243178528758.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45ee7412-a593-11f1-93a6-2d6b79c37be8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:34:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c71ef2e6-a593-11f1-b096-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26243178528758.jpg">© Dar Yasin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Xi, Putin hold talks ahead of Shanghai Cooperation Organization summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260831-xi-putin-hold-talks-ahead-of-shanghai-cooperation-organization-summit</link><description>
Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russia's Vladimir Putin are among the heads of state attending a Shanghai Cooperation Organization summit taking place in Kyrgyzstan.  Iran's president Masoud Pezeshkian is also in attendance, where he held bilateral talks with India's Narendra Modi.  Marking its 25th anniversary this year, the SCO has strengthened trade ties among its members as the bloc looks to present an alternative to the US-led world order. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/474e1ea4-a57d-11f1-a079-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15294708146a95e88aba5648-08542646.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/474e1ea4-a57d-11f1-a079-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15294708146a95e88aba5648-08542646.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a4cfdb30-a57d-11f1-b7c8-a577c0d2835a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:51:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump threatens to ‘hit Iran hard’ as strikes resume after month-long lull</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull</link><description>
President Donald Trump said Monday that the US would hit back against Iranian attacks on US targets in the Middle East, according to a Fox News reporter. The Iranian attacks were themselves a response to US strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first flare-up in a month.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6a05eba-a57a-11f1-a76a-fb7aabece8fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:36:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg">© via Reuters/Wana News Agency</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenya airport staff strike delays thousands of passengers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-airport-staff-strike-delays-thousands-of-passengers</link><description>
In tonight's edition, a workers' strike at Kenya's main airport leaves travelers grounded. Also, Ghanaian cocoa farmers are ramping up their pushback against a new law preventing them from using their land for anything else without permission. And in Tunisia, Sidi Bou Said's been recognized by UNESCO as being important to global heritage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6e5a218-a578-11f1-8eec-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/WB220715-O-01-20260831-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6e5a218-a578-11f1-8eec-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/WB220715-O-01-20260831-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37ba1456-a579-11f1-9c74-fb7aabece8fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:20:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Marine Le Pen's National Rally plans to "sanction" the wearing of the veil with a fine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/marine-le-pen-s-national-rally-plans-to-sanction-the-wearing-of-the-veil-with-a-fine</link><description>
The National Rally plans to "penalize the wearing of the Islamic veil" with "a fine" if it comes to power, MP Jean-Philippe Tanguy, Marine Le Pen's lieutenant in the presidential election, stated on Sunday. "We will obviously fight Islamist ideology and we will penalize the wearing of the veil, also in solidarity with all the women around the world who are forced to wear it and who die for this freedom," the MP said. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84518dfc-a52a-11f1-984c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T154621Z-1088021487-RC237NAUVKIC-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84518dfc-a52a-11f1-984c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T154621Z-1088021487-RC237NAUVKIC-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f77b2e8-a573-11f1-b1c3-fb7aabece8fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Nepal disaster: fake and AI images flood social media as deaths mount</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-disaster-fake-and-ai-images-flood-social-media-as-deaths-mount</link><description>
As deadly floods hit the Nepal-China border, social media is being flooded with fake and misleading footage. In Truth or Fake, Vedika Bahl goes through viral videos falsely linked to the disaster, including AI-generated content and old recycled footage from India, Chile and Alaska. Some posts have racked up millions of views online, exploiting the tragedy to drive engagement for easy clicks or further perpetuate conspiracy theories. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e5ae9d8-a570-11f1-9682-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-499210196a95d2ac205d05-65537713.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3e5ae9d8-a570-11f1-9682-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-499210196a95d2ac205d05-65537713.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96bbde54-a56e-11f1-ab3b-01902f20a226</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:00:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron seals €4.3-bn French frigate deal in Sweden</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-macron-seals-%E2%82%AC4-3-bn-french-frigate-deal-in-sweden</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron on Monday oversaw the signing of a 4.3-billion-euro ($4.9 billon) deal for Sweden to buy four French frigates as France and Sweden seek to tighten cooperation against a backdrop of growing Russian threats. Sweden is racing to boost its defences after Russia invaded Ukraine in 2022, with the Nordic country becoming a NATO member two years later. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2a337c-a53e-11f1-9c98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13517109716a957fe9a180a3-87110240.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2a337c-a53e-11f1-9c98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13517109716a957fe9a180a3-87110240.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1b67e02-a56d-11f1-89b4-01902f20a226</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:28:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Former French prime minister Édouard Balladur dies at 97</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260831-former-french-prime-minister-%C3%A9douard-balladur-dies-at-97</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">dff77c3e-a56b-11f1-9957-01902f20a226</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:47:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Former French PM Édouard Balladur, once defeated by ally Jacques Chirac, dies at 97</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260831-former-french-prime-minister-%C3%A9douard-balladur-dies-at-97</link><description>
Édouard Balladur, who served as prime minister of France from 1993 to 1995, died on Monday at the age of 97. He led a "cohabitation" government under Socialist president François Mitterrand before waging a bitter battle for the presidency against his friend Jacques Chirac in 1995 – a race he ultimately lost.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d353db6-e42d-11e9-9f39-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/balladur-.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d353db6-e42d-11e9-9f39-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/balladur-.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a6bcd0e-a56c-11f1-aa0a-01902f20a226</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:46:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d353db6-e42d-11e9-9f39-005056bff430/w:1024/p:16x9/balladur-.jpg">Éric Feferberg, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump vows to hit back 'hard' after first exchange of fire with Iran in weeks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks</link><description>
Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran "hard" after the two foes traded fire for the first time in over a month, while Iran's president warned that more fighting with the US was not in his country's interest. After six months of war, the foes remain at an impasse, with Iran keeping the strategic Strait of Hormuz closed and the US persisting with a naval counter-blockade of Iran. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61eaaa56-8a5d-11f1-8f74-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C39X7A2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61eaaa56-8a5d-11f1-8f74-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C39X7A2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d277974-a56a-11f1-9374-435f773a4b38</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:37:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hundreds feared stuck in hydropower tunnels as flood deaths surpass 950 in Nepal and China</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-feared-stuck-in-hydropower-tunnels-as-flood-deaths-surpass-950-in-nepal-and-china</link><description>
Rescuers raced Monday to free hundreds of workers believed to be trapped in tunnels at hydropower sites that were buried in mud by catastrophic flooding on the Nepal-China border, as the death toll climbed and increasingly desperate families searched for missing loved ones. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe94334-a569-11f1-a255-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-200222-200417-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abe94334-a569-11f1-a255-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260831-200222-200417-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1588ae6-a569-11f1-8eca-0d645d89d448</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:34:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Raising the Altalena: Netanyahu digs up sunken 1948 arms ship in ‘pre-election stunt’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt</link><description>
A ship carrying arms for a right-wing militia, the Altalena was sunk 78 years ago off the coast of Tel Aviv at the orders of Israel’s founders. The discovery of its wreckage last week has given the country’s right-wing government ammunition to target the left and attempt to redirect the campaign for legislative elections in October.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03fb2ff4-a54e-11f1-ba53-494925e89fd0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:54:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg">© Wikimedia Creative Commons</source><dc:creator>Stéphanie TROUILLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France targets Shein and Temu with new fast fashion levy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260831-france-targets-shein-and-temu-with-new-fast-fashion-levy</link><description><![CDATA[
Starting this week, France will charge a penalty on cheaply made clothing sold by ultra-fast fashion retailers, with the fee reaching nearly €20 per item by 2030. Aimed at platforms like Shein, Temu and AliExpress, the levy follows a June law targeting disposable fashion's environmental toll, though rival brands like H&M and Zara are exempt.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b81f0872-a55b-11f1-bfba-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T095850Z-1200926585-RC27HIARHQ0D-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b81f0872-a55b-11f1-bfba-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T095850Z-1200926585-RC27HIARHQ0D-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a3534ae-a554-11f1-b888-bf56321c7dab</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:55:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b81f0872-a55b-11f1-bfba-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T095850Z-1200926585-RC27HIARHQ0D-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg">© Jorge Silva, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal floods 'unprecedented', requires new 'engineering approaches, risk-sensitive urban planning'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nepal-floods-unprecedented-requires-new-engineering-approaches-risk-sensitive-urban-planning</link><description>
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Basanta Raj Adhikari, Director of the Center for Disaster Studies at Tribhuvan University’s Institute of Engineering.  He describes the disaster as an illustration of the limits of conventional prevention in the Himalayas. With flood velocities estimated at 170 to 180 kilometres per hour and hazards ranging from ice and snow avalanches to glacial lake outburst floods, he argues that comprehensive monitoring of Nepal’s exceptionally steep and complex mountain terrain is effectively impossible. Yet Adhikari’s analysis is not fatalistic. Instead, he shifts the emphasis from attempting to predict every extreme event toward risk-informed adaptation. Nepal, he argues, should identify high-risk hotspots through satellite observation, supplement these with ground-based monitoring and early-warning systems, and incorporate that knowledge into risk-sensitive land-use planning.
